  "comment": "The GATE input is a level test at 1V rather than an edge, so it holds the burst on but never advances the step counter: step counting is gated on trigon, which only ON and TOGGLE set. The clock measurement is kept in whole samples (timer/goal are incremented once per process call), so the multiplied rate follows the sample rate exactly and a change of sample rate is absorbed. The x4 switch has no configParam of its own; Rack's Module::config gives it the default 0 to 1 range and a default of 0, so it comes up off and its tooltip has no name."
